{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-245", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/245", "wordCount": 4009, "segments": [{"start": 6.0, "text": "Hello, I'm Yuval Kossovsky"}, {"start": 8.0, "text": "and I'd like to welcome you to"}, {"start": 9.0, "text": "the Indoor Maps Program."}, {"start": 11.0, "text": "Perhaps, you are the owner of a"}, {"start": 12.0, "text": "large hospital, office tower,"}, {"start": 14.0, "text": "stadium or museum and are"}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "looking to add indoor maps and"}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "positioning to your own consumer"}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "or enterprise apps."}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "Or perhaps you are the owner of"}, {"start": 23.0, "text": "an airport, shopping mall or"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "other facility with large"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "numbers of public visitors and"}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "you'd like your indoor map and"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "locations to be part of the"}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "Apple Maps' indoor experience."}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "This session will have something"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "of interest to each of you."}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "Outdoor location services have"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "become embedded into our cities,"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "our travel, our daily commutes,"}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "and even our social"}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "interactivity."}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "And people are beginning to"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "expect a location experience"}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "everywhere, including the"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "indoors."}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "In addition to a digital version"}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "of the well-known You-Are-Here"}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "map, there are many compelling"}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "consumer, operations and"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "enterprise use cases that have"}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "indoor maps and indoor"}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "positioning at their core."}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "Air travel, for example, can be"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "incredibly stressful when you"}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "don't know where to park, where"}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "the security line is, where the"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "gates are, or how long it will"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "take to get from where you are"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "to where you want to go."}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "A map updated in real time that"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "shows you where your gate is,"}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "where you are and how much free"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "time you have for shopping or a"}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "quick bite before your flight"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "would make for a much more"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "pleasant journey."}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "Looking at the operation side of"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "the building, a staff member"}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "might need to locate a piece of"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "equipment for routine"}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "maintenance or to service an"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "outage."}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "Using indoor maps and indoor"}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "positioning, the equipment"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "report can be tagged with an"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "accurate latitude, longitude and"}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "floor level."}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "Then the nearest technician with"}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "the right skills to resolve the"}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "issue can be guided directly to"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "the location to begin work,"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "providing an incredible boost in"}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "operations efficiency."}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "Finally, consider that first"}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "responders have only moments to"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "study a building layout before"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "deciding on a plan of action."}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "Typically, the only available"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "indoor maps are on paper and are"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "not current."}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "Using electronically maintained"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "indoor maps to show the location"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "of the incidents, as well as the"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "location of the responders"}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "inside the buildings, can"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "greatly reduce response times,"}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "and in some cases, even save"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "lives."}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "These three scenarios are just a"}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "few examples of what can be done"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "with indoor maps and indoor"}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "positioning through the Apple"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "Indoor Maps Program."}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "The Indoor Maps Program enables"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "organizations with large public"}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "and private spaces to create"}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "standard space indoor maps,"}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "enable indoor positioning and"}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "create stunning indoor maps in"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "their own apps and websites."}, {"start": 165.0, "text": "This session will discuss the"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "overall workflow for"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "accomplishing these tasks and"}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "provide some guidance in the"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "form of best practices for"}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "success at each step."}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "At the core of the program is"}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "the Indoor Mapping Data Format,"}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "or IMDF."}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "This is Apple specification for"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "modeling indoor spaces and is"}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "represented as a set of GeoJSON"}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "files."}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "Many of your favorite mapping in"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "GIS platforms are already"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "supporting the creation and"}, {"start": 196.0, "text": "editing of IMDF as it has"}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "quickly become the de facto"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "exchange standard for indoor"}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "data."}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "Let's take a deeper look at the"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "Indoor Maps Program."}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "Building and property owners"}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "start by converting their CAD,"}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "BIM or GIS files to IMDF using"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "industry standard tools."}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "Then they can use that IMDF map"}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "and developer tools from Apple"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "to display indoor maps in their"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "own consumer and enterprise"}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "apps."}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "In this simple case, displaying"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "the IMDF in an app is something"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "that any developer can do easily"}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "by themselves using MapKit and"}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "MapKit JS tools."}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "Because building and"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "understanding IMDF can be a bit"}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "more complicated, there is the"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "IMDF Sandbox, a tool for"}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "visualization, archive"}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "inspection, editing and"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "experimentation with an IMDF"}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "archive."}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "Companies that own large public"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "and private spaces, such as"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "airports, shopping centers,"}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "arenas, hospitals, universities"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "and private office buildings,"}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "are welcome to register their"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "organization for the Indoor Maps"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "Program, create IMDF maps using"}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "industry standard tools,"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "validate those IMDF maps in the"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "Sandbox, enable Apple indoor"}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "positioning and then use MapKit"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "and MapKit JS to display indoor"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "maps and indoor positioning in"}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "their apps and websites."}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "Highly trafficked locations,"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "such as airports and shopping"}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "centers, may also want the"}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "public indoor maps of their"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "buildings to be included in"}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "Apple Maps."}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "Any participant in the Indoor"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "Maps Program can activate indoor"}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "positioning for their building"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "and use the IMDF maps in their"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "apps and websites."}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "Let's go into more detail about"}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "the process for joining the"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "Indoor Maps Program, managing"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "your organization's account and"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "claiming your building"}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "locations."}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "Navigate your browser to"}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "register.apple.com/indoor to"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "learn more about the program and"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "get links to tools, information"}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "and documentation."}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "Click on Get Started to begin"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "enrolling your organization."}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "When an organization enrolls for"}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "the Indoor Maps Program at Apple"}, {"start": 325.0, "text": "Business Register, an in-depth"}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "check is done on their business"}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "information."}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "The individuals performing the"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "sign up must have emails"}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "connected to the organizational"}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "domain, and all of the primary"}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "contacts must be employees or"}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "registered agents of the"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "company."}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "Once the organization is"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "validated and approved, the"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "administrator is able to manage"}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "their team members through the"}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "controls on the right."}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "Tapping or clicking on team"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "members reveals the list of"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "members, and tapping on the plus"}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "sign reveals a dialog for both"}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "individuals and entire"}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "organizations to participate in"}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "this organization."}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "The invitees can be assigned any"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "number of five different roles"}, {"start": 368.0, "text": "and given access to the entire"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "catalog of venues or selected"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "individual locations."}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "This granular control enables an"}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "organization to easily outsource"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "IMDF mapmaking and survey to"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "partners on a venue-by-venue"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "basis or across the"}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "organization."}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "System integrators wishing to"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "make IMDF to survey for indoor"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "positioning or build indoor apps"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "for their clients should get"}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "invited to an organization,"}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "rather than try to claim a"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "client's buildings on their"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "behalf."}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "And that is team management."}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "Claiming locations for an"}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "organization is easy."}, {"start": 408.0, "text": "Keep in mind that the claims can"}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "only be made for your own"}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "properties, not on behalf of"}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "others."}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "Click on Indoor Maps under"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "Connected Services, tap the plus"}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "button and select your location."}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "Depending on the categorization"}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "of the building, you'll be"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "presented with different options"}, {"start": 424.0, "text": "for how to proceed."}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "Buildings that are private"}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "locations are not eligible to"}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "have their indoor maps display"}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "in Apple Maps."}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "Properties such as airports will"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "be asked for permission to"}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "display their indoor maps in"}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "Apple Maps."}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "Once the location claim is"}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "approved, you can upload an IMDF"}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "and the validator will begin"}, {"start": 444.0, "text": "analyzing the file"}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "automatically."}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "After a few minutes, you'll"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "receive an email indicating that"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "validation is complete."}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "There will be a link to the"}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "validation report, where you can"}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "see any errors that blocked"}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "acceptance of the file or any"}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "warnings which indicate"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "conditions that need further"}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "examination."}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "You can use the embedded link to"}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "the IMDF Sandbox to view the"}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "IMDF file, make quick edits if"}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "needed."}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "Once an IMDF is error free in"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "the validator, it will move to"}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "georeferencing and evaluation."}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "To ensure accurate indoor"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "positioning, the IMDF must have"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "walkable areas for survey and be"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "aligned with the Apple satellite"}, {"start": 483.0, "text": "imagery."}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "The indoor team will manually"}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "check the georeferencing of your"}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "IMDF and do a cursory check for"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "defects in the IMDF that cannot"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "be surfaced in the validator."}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "If any changes are made to the"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "file, they will be saved into a"}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "new IMDF, which will be made"}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "available under Download"}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "Georeference to IMDF, along with"}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "a report indicating what work"}, {"start": 506.0, "text": "was done."}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "Let's review the best practices"}, {"start": 508.0, "text": "for joining and participating in"}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "the Apple Indoor Maps Program."}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "While anyone can make an IMDF"}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "map and display it in their app"}, {"start": 516.0, "text": "and website using MapKit and"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "MapKit JS, the Indoor Maps"}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "Program and enabling Apple"}, {"start": 522.0, "text": "indoor positioning is for owners"}, {"start": 524.0, "text": "of large properties."}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "Some measures of large include"}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "50 square meters, 5 million"}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "annual visitors, or entire"}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "office buildings."}, {"start": 532.0, "text": "The individuals enrolling must"}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "be part of the organization and"}, {"start": 536.0, "text": "must provide enough information"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "to verify the organization"}, {"start": 539.0, "text": "details."}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "If there's an existing account,"}, {"start": 542.0, "text": "the current account admins will"}, {"start": 544.0, "text": "be notified of the new enrollees"}, {"start": 546.0, "text": "and asked to invite them"}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "directly."}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "This ensures the organization"}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "maintains control of all"}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "members."}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "Some locations are eligible for"}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "display in Apple Maps."}, {"start": 556.0, "text": "However, the indoor map will"}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "remain private unless permission"}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "is given."}, {"start": 562.0, "text": "IMDF is the basis for the map"}, {"start": 564.0, "text": "used to display in your app and"}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "website and to enable indoor"}, {"start": 568.0, "text": "positioning."}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "To create an IMDF, work with"}, {"start": 571.0, "text": "your facilities team to"}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "investigate the offerings"}, {"start": 574.0, "text": "available from companies, like"}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "Safe Software, Autodesk, Esri,"}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "and other GIS and BIM tool"}, {"start": 581.0, "text": "platforms."}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "Let's take a deeper look at"}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "IMDF."}, {"start": 585.0, "text": "To understand how IMDF is"}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "constructed, we should first"}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "look at the general components"}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "of a building floor plan."}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "An indoor map like a regular map"}, {"start": 594.0, "text": "is comprised of many layers."}, {"start": 596.0, "text": "Each of these layers may contain"}, {"start": 598.0, "text": "several features."}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "Let's break down this building"}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "map, for example."}, {"start": 602.0, "text": "Simplistically, the base of an"}, {"start": 603.0, "text": "indoor map is the building"}, {"start": 605.0, "text": "ground footprint, or the size"}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "and shape of the physical"}, {"start": 608.0, "text": "building plus the"}, {"start": 609.0, "text": "GeoCoordinates, where it sits on"}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "the earth."}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "Indoor locations are still on"}, {"start": 613.0, "text": "the earth."}, {"start": 614.0, "text": "And to handle the movement of"}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "people in and out of the"}, {"start": 616.0, "text": "building, an indoor data model"}, {"start": 618.0, "text": "has to account for this fact."}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "Georeferencing of the building"}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "is the solution."}, {"start": 623.0, "text": "The next step is to add a level."}, {"start": 625.0, "text": "Again, simplistically, we can"}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "use the ground floor or ordinal"}, {"start": 629.0, "text": "zero for our example."}, {"start": 632.0, "text": "The level is entirely covered by"}, {"start": 634.0, "text": "some form of what we call a"}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "unit, for example, a room, a"}, {"start": 638.0, "text": "walkway, an elevator or an"}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "escalator."}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "Anything that occupies space on"}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "the level is defined with"}, {"start": 644.0, "text": "geometry and a category of some"}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "kind."}, {"start": 647.0, "text": "Rooms typically have doors or"}, {"start": 649.0, "text": "what we call openings."}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "And then within the units, there"}, {"start": 653.0, "text": "are also other objects, such as"}, {"start": 655.0, "text": "kiosks."}, {"start": 656.0, "text": "They're typically in the walkway"}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "unit of a shopping center or"}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "mall."}, {"start": 660.0, "text": "Next, there are labels which are"}, {"start": 662.0, "text": "applied to the units, such as"}, {"start": 663.0, "text": "the name of a business that"}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "occupies a room."}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "Icons are used to mark the"}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "location of amenities of"}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "interest, such as an elevator or"}, {"start": 673.0, "text": "a restroom. At the Jurassic Table"}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "restaurant, there is also a"}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "delimited area that acts as a"}, {"start": 679.0, "text": "virtual boundary, which extends"}, {"start": 681.0, "text": "outside of the walls of the"}, {"start": 683.0, "text": "actual unit."}, {"start": 684.0, "text": "This could be post security in"}, {"start": 686.0, "text": "an airport or the food court in"}, {"start": 688.0, "text": "a mall."}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "And these are some of the"}, {"start": 690.0, "text": "constructs that make a good"}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "indoor map format, such as IMDF."}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "Underlying the format are rules"}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "on how to consistently capture"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "information about the physical"}, {"start": 700.0, "text": "spaces and the business purpose"}, {"start": 703.0, "text": "of those spaces into an easy to"}, {"start": 705.0, "text": "understand hierarchy."}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "Let's take a look at some of the"}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "required features and some"}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "optional elements that make up"}, {"start": 712.0, "text": "an IMDF archive."}, {"start": 713.0, "text": "There are three core files that"}, {"start": 716.0, "text": "provide the base information of"}, {"start": 717.0, "text": "the venue, the manifest, which"}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "has some administrative detail,"}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "the address, which provides the"}, {"start": 723.0, "text": "postal address, and the venue"}, {"start": 725.0, "text": "layer that describes the overall"}, {"start": 727.0, "text": "shape of the location."}, {"start": 728.0, "text": "The property is then extended by"}, {"start": 730.0, "text": "the building layer, and its"}, {"start": 732.0, "text": "associated footprint layers"}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "which bring details to the"}, {"start": 735.0, "text": "physical building."}, {"start": 737.0, "text": "Working our way deeper in, the"}, {"start": 739.0, "text": "levels within the building are"}, {"start": 740.0, "text": "defined."}, {"start": 742.0, "text": "The level is then entirely"}, {"start": 743.0, "text": "covered in units, which are"}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "associated with openings, such"}, {"start": 747.0, "text": "as doorways."}, {"start": 749.0, "text": "The level also has logical area"}, {"start": 751.0, "text": "groupings, like sections and"}, {"start": 753.0, "text": "trigger regions like geofences."}, {"start": 756.0, "text": "Then kiosks and fixtures are"}, {"start": 759.0, "text": "placed."}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "Amenities and their associated"}, {"start": 763.0, "text": "data are assigned to the units,"}, {"start": 765.0, "text": "and finally, anchors are used"}, {"start": 767.0, "text": "for positioning references and"}, {"start": 769.0, "text": "unit addresses with additional"}, {"start": 771.0, "text": "data blocks, such as the"}, {"start": 772.0, "text": "occupant, providing the occupant"}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "name and phone number and"}, {"start": 776.0, "text": "related data."}, {"start": 777.0, "text": "And that is how the hierarchy is"}, {"start": 779.0, "text": "set up."}, {"start": 780.0, "text": "You can learn more by reading"}, {"start": 782.0, "text": "the Indoor Mapping Data"}, {"start": 783.0, "text": "Specification in detail."}, {"start": 785.0, "text": "But what is IMDF to the"}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "developer's eye?"}, {"start": 789.0, "text": "An IMDF is an archive made up of"}, {"start": 791.0, "text": "multiple GeoJSON files and the"}, {"start": 793.0, "text": "multiple files we discussed."}, {"start": 796.0, "text": "This is a GeoJSON file."}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "And as you can see here, there's"}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "a unique UUID provided to the"}, {"start": 802.0, "text": "specific feature type of level."}, {"start": 805.0, "text": "The public can access this"}, {"start": 807.0, "text": "building so the restriction"}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "property is set to null and it"}, {"start": 811.0, "text": "is indoors."}, {"start": 812.0, "text": "This is level one in the"}, {"start": 813.0, "text": "building."}, {"start": 814.0, "text": "And what you see printed on the"}, {"start": 816.0, "text": "elevator button is L1."}, {"start": 817.0, "text": "Importantly, we see that this"}, {"start": 820.0, "text": "level is associated to a single"}, {"start": 822.0, "text": "building ID and it has a good"}, {"start": 824.0, "text": "geometrical shape as described"}, {"start": 826.0, "text": "here."}, {"start": 827.0, "text": "All in all, a comprehensive set"}, {"start": 829.0, "text": "of information in a simple text"}, {"start": 832.0, "text": "file."}, {"start": 833.0, "text": "Let's review some of the"}, {"start": 834.0, "text": "important elements in"}, {"start": 835.0, "text": "understanding and crafting an"}, {"start": 837.0, "text": "Indoor Mapping Data Format"}, {"start": 839.0, "text": "archive."}, {"start": 840.0, "text": "It is important to understand"}, {"start": 842.0, "text": "how the layers relate and where"}, {"start": 844.0, "text": "the data for each element is"}, {"start": 845.0, "text": "surfaced."}, {"start": 846.0, "text": "It is important to ensure that"}, {"start": 848.0, "text": "the IMDF is complete, even from"}, {"start": 850.0, "text": "proof of concept deliveries and"}, {"start": 852.0, "text": "that the units cover the entire"}, {"start": 854.0, "text": "building."}, {"start": 855.0, "text": "Everything on the level is a"}, {"start": 857.0, "text": "unit, including walkways which"}, {"start": 859.0, "text": "have their own category."}, {"start": 861.0, "text": "Speaking of categories, they are"}, {"start": 863.0, "text": "critical to a good map and good"}, {"start": 865.0, "text": "rendering behavior."}, {"start": 867.0, "text": "Openings are important for both"}, {"start": 869.0, "text": "location accuracy and proper"}, {"start": 871.0, "text": "routing and should be included"}, {"start": 873.0, "text": "to make it easier for those with"}, {"start": 874.0, "text": "mobility and site challenges."}, {"start": 877.0, "text": "Occupants should have unique"}, {"start": 878.0, "text": "addresses and IDs for tracking"}, {"start": 881.0, "text": "and updates of names."}, {"start": 882.0, "text": "Finally, when making the IMDF,"}, {"start": 885.0, "text": "consider the indoor survey."}, {"start": 887.0, "text": "Large spaces are hard to get"}, {"start": 889.0, "text": "accurate orientation."}, {"start": 890.0, "text": "Even if your map doesn't need"}, {"start": 892.0, "text": "the information, including"}, {"start": 894.0, "text": "notable landmarks or orienting"}, {"start": 895.0, "text": "information like columns, will"}, {"start": 897.0, "text": "make it much easier for getting"}, {"start": 899.0, "text": "proper calibration during the"}, {"start": 900.0, "text": "indoor positioning survey, and"}, {"start": 902.0, "text": "consequently better accuracy"}, {"start": 904.0, "text": "after."}, {"start": 905.0, "text": "And that's creating the IMDF."}, {"start": 908.0, "text": "Next, let's look at validation."}, {"start": 910.0, "text": "As I mentioned earlier, when an"}, {"start": 912.0, "text": "IMDF is uploaded into the"}, {"start": 914.0, "text": "organization's account, it is"}, {"start": 916.0, "text": "electronically validated and a"}, {"start": 918.0, "text": "report is provided with a"}, {"start": 919.0, "text": "detailed analysis."}, {"start": 921.0, "text": "While this may be easy for"}, {"start": 922.0, "text": "well-schooled GIS professionals"}, {"start": 924.0, "text": "to consume, we thought there"}, {"start": 926.0, "text": "might be an easier way to work"}, {"start": 928.0, "text": "with this sort of information."}, {"start": 930.0, "text": "The IMDF Sandbox is a"}, {"start": 931.0, "text": "browser-based tool for"}, {"start": 933.0, "text": "visualizing IMDF, searching the"}, {"start": 936.0, "text": "IMDF file, observing the"}, {"start": 938.0, "text": "validations and making simple"}, {"start": 940.0, "text": "edits."}, {"start": 941.0, "text": "I have a sample IMDF archive"}, {"start": 943.0, "text": "data set opened here."}, {"start": 945.0, "text": "First of all, you can see the"}, {"start": 946.0, "text": "map."}, {"start": 947.0, "text": "This is rendering the IMDF data"}, {"start": 948.0, "text": "to show you how it looks."}, {"start": 951.0, "text": "There's a level picker for"}, {"start": 952.0, "text": "switching between levels and a"}, {"start": 955.0, "text": "compass to show you the"}, {"start": 957.0, "text": "orientation."}, {"start": 958.0, "text": "On the left, you'll find a"}, {"start": 962.0, "text": "directory that will help you"}, {"start": 963.0, "text": "browse and navigate the data"}, {"start": 965.0, "text": "with quick access to all the"}, {"start": 967.0, "text": "businesses and services."}, {"start": 976.0, "text": "Or browse the data by building"}, {"start": 978.0, "text": "or by level."}, {"start": 988.0, "text": "At the top, there's a search bar"}, {"start": 991.0, "text": "that lets you search for"}, {"start": 992.0, "text": "anything and everything within"}, {"start": 994.0, "text": "this data set."}, {"start": 1002.0, "text": "At the top of the panel at the"}, {"start": 1003.0, "text": "Home, you'll also see a link to"}, {"start": 1005.0, "text": "all the validation errors and"}, {"start": 1007.0, "text": "warnings triggered by this data"}, {"start": 1009.0, "text": "set."}, {"start": 1010.0, "text": "The validation engine is the"}, {"start": 1011.0, "text": "same tool in use when an IMDF is"}, {"start": 1014.0, "text": "uploaded to the Indoor Maps"}, {"start": 1016.0, "text": "Program, but the results are"}, {"start": 1018.0, "text": "interpreted and visualized by"}, {"start": 1020.0, "text": "the Sandbox."}, {"start": 1021.0, "text": "In this case, there are no"}, {"start": 1022.0, "text": "errors, but just warnings."}, {"start": 1025.0, "text": "Warnings are present because the"}, {"start": 1026.0, "text": "validator identifies a scenario"}, {"start": 1028.0, "text": "that could be an error or could"}, {"start": 1030.0, "text": "be ignored."}, {"start": 1031.0, "text": "Depending on your business use"}, {"start": 1033.0, "text": "case, it is important to have"}, {"start": 1035.0, "text": "someone with an understanding of"}, {"start": 1036.0, "text": "the IMDF specification and the"}, {"start": 1039.0, "text": "business use case review"}, {"start": 1040.0, "text": "warnings generated by the"}, {"start": 1042.0, "text": "validator to make a decision on"}, {"start": 1044.0, "text": "their importance."}, {"start": 1045.0, "text": "Let's take a look at how the"}, {"start": 1047.0, "text": "IMDF Sandbox can be used to"}, {"start": 1049.0, "text": "discover errors and do some"}, {"start": 1051.0, "text": "light editing."}, {"start": 1052.0, "text": "I've introduced a few errors"}, {"start": 1054.0, "text": "into my sample data to show you"}, {"start": 1055.0, "text": "how this works."}, {"start": 1056.0, "text": "When I first load the IMDF"}, {"start": 1058.0, "text": "archive, the Sandbox shows me"}, {"start": 1060.0, "text": "errors."}, {"start": 1061.0, "text": "The warnings are shown in the"}, {"start": 1062.0, "text": "other tab."}, {"start": 1063.0, "text": "In order for my IMDF to be"}, {"start": 1065.0, "text": "accepted into the Indoor Maps"}, {"start": 1066.0, "text": "Program, it cannot have any"}, {"start": 1068.0, "text": "errors."}, {"start": 1069.0, "text": "So, let's take a closer look and"}, {"start": 1071.0, "text": "get these resolved."}, {"start": 1072.0, "text": "First, we can see that there are"}, {"start": 1073.0, "text": "overlapping units."}, {"start": 1075.0, "text": "In IMDF, units should never"}, {"start": 1076.0, "text": "overlap."}, {"start": 1077.0, "text": "So this is an error."}, {"start": 1079.0, "text": "Taking a closer look, the"}, {"start": 1081.0, "text": "Sandbox tells us that there are"}, {"start": 1082.0, "text": "two instances of this error in"}, {"start": 1084.0, "text": "this data set."}, {"start": 1085.0, "text": "By clicking one or the other,"}, {"start": 1087.0, "text": "the map zooms to that particular"}, {"start": 1088.0, "text": "location and highlights which"}, {"start": 1090.0, "text": "units overlap."}, {"start": 1092.0, "text": "Here, it is the blue unit and"}, {"start": 1094.0, "text": "the yellow unit overlapping with"}, {"start": 1096.0, "text": "the overlapping areas shown in"}, {"start": 1098.0, "text": "orange."}, {"start": 1099.0, "text": "The Sandbox provides me with an"}, {"start": 1100.0, "text": "easy option to remove the"}, {"start": 1102.0, "text": "overlap by simply removing the"}, {"start": 1104.0, "text": "overlapping area from one or the"}, {"start": 1106.0, "text": "other."}, {"start": 1107.0, "text": "I have chosen to remove the"}, {"start": 1109.0, "text": "overlap from the blue unit,"}, {"start": 1110.0, "text": "because then both units are nice"}, {"start": 1112.0, "text": "and rectangular."}, {"start": 1113.0, "text": "And now, it is fixed."}, {"start": 1115.0, "text": "Let's take a look at the other"}, {"start": 1116.0, "text": "overlapping units error."}, {"start": 1118.0, "text": "It seems this elevator is too"}, {"start": 1120.0, "text": "large. So I'm going to remove that"}, {"start": 1121.0, "text": "overlap from the elevator unit."}, {"start": 1123.0, "text": "And now, both errors have been"}, {"start": 1125.0, "text": "fixed."}, {"start": 1126.0, "text": "There is now one other error I"}, {"start": 1128.0, "text": "need to quickly resolve with the"}, {"start": 1130.0, "text": "unit being outside the reference"}, {"start": 1131.0, "text": "level."}, {"start": 1132.0, "text": "You can see the orange area"}, {"start": 1134.0, "text": "outside the level looks to be"}, {"start": 1135.0, "text": "some sort of drawing error that"}, {"start": 1137.0, "text": "was picked up when the file was"}, {"start": 1138.0, "text": "digitized."}, {"start": 1140.0, "text": "I removed that area from the"}, {"start": 1141.0, "text": "level and the entire file is now"}, {"start": 1143.0, "text": "free from errors."}, {"start": 1145.0, "text": "Because all of the work in the"}, {"start": 1147.0, "text": "Sandbox is done locally in the"}, {"start": 1148.0, "text": "browser, I will have to click on"}, {"start": 1150.0, "text": "Download the IMDF at the top"}, {"start": 1153.0, "text": "right of the screen and save a"}, {"start": 1154.0, "text": "copy in order to keep these"}, {"start": 1156.0, "text": "changes for use in register and"}, {"start": 1158.0, "text": "adding back into my content"}, {"start": 1159.0, "text": "management system."}, {"start": 1161.0, "text": "To recap, best practices for"}, {"start": 1163.0, "text": "IMDF validation."}, {"start": 1165.0, "text": "The same validation tools are"}, {"start": 1167.0, "text": "available when uploading your"}, {"start": 1168.0, "text": "files to the Indoor Maps Program"}, {"start": 1171.0, "text": "and the IMDF Sandbox."}, {"start": 1173.0, "text": "They check the accuracy and"}, {"start": 1174.0, "text": "integrity of your IMDF to the"}, {"start": 1176.0, "text": "limit of the business use case."}, {"start": 1179.0, "text": "Warnings are surfaced when a"}, {"start": 1180.0, "text": "condition can apply to multiple"}, {"start": 1182.0, "text": "use cases."}, {"start": 1183.0, "text": "After validation, the IMDF is"}, {"start": 1186.0, "text": "checked manually for accurate"}, {"start": 1187.0, "text": "placement on the earth or"}, {"start": 1189.0, "text": "georeferencing to ensure"}, {"start": 1191.0, "text": "accurate indoor positioning when"}, {"start": 1192.0, "text": "indoor positioning is enabled."}, {"start": 1195.0, "text": "With IMDF Sandbox, you can"}, {"start": 1196.0, "text": "easily look at complex IMDFs and"}, {"start": 1199.0, "text": "see the details, identifying"}, {"start": 1201.0, "text": "fixed errors and then save the"}, {"start": 1203.0, "text": "files."}, {"start": 1204.0, "text": "All of this work is done locally"}, {"start": 1206.0, "text": "in your browser and is not"}, {"start": 1208.0, "text": "shared with Apple."}, {"start": 1209.0, "text": "The IMDF Sandbox is available"}, {"start": 1211.0, "text": "for anyone with an Apple ID and"}, {"start": 1214.0, "text": "not just building owners in the"}, {"start": 1216.0, "text": "Indoor Maps Program."}, {"start": 1217.0, "text": "And that is IMDF validation."}, {"start": 1221.0, "text": "So, now, we know how to join the"}, {"start": 1222.0, "text": "Indoor Maps Program, create an"}, {"start": 1224.0, "text": "IMDF and validate it."}, {"start": 1227.0, "text": "The next step is to enable Apple"}, {"start": 1229.0, "text": "indoor positioning."}, {"start": 1231.0, "text": "But first, we need to understand"}, {"start": 1233.0, "text": "just how Apple indoor"}, {"start": 1234.0, "text": "positioning works."}, {"start": 1236.0, "text": "Imagine a still pond and a drop"}, {"start": 1238.0, "text": "of rain falls on the surface of"}, {"start": 1240.0, "text": "the water."}, {"start": 1241.0, "text": "The ripples caused by the"}, {"start": 1242.0, "text": "raindrop are much like the"}, {"start": 1243.0, "text": "signal coming from an access"}, {"start": 1245.0, "text": "point. With one drop, one set of"}, {"start": 1247.0, "text": "ripples."}, {"start": 1248.0, "text": "But with multiple raindrops, you"}, {"start": 1250.0, "text": "get many ripples which produce"}, {"start": 1251.0, "text": "waves that intersect with each"}, {"start": 1253.0, "text": "other, lay a grid over the"}, {"start": 1254.0, "text": "waves, and inside each box,"}, {"start": 1257.0, "text": "there will be a unique texture"}, {"start": 1258.0, "text": "pattern of ripples or what we"}, {"start": 1260.0, "text": "call the fingerprint."}, {"start": 1262.0, "text": "The IMDF map provides the"}, {"start": 1264.0, "text": "latitude, longitude and floor"}, {"start": 1266.0, "text": "coordinates for each box in the"}, {"start": 1267.0, "text": "grid, allowing the location"}, {"start": 1269.0, "text": "service to create a pairing"}, {"start": 1271.0, "text": "between the coordinates and the"}, {"start": 1273.0, "text": "fingerprint."}, {"start": 1274.0, "text": "When your iPhone or iPad is"}, {"start": 1275.0, "text": "entering the building, the"}, {"start": 1277.0, "text": "fingerprint is downloaded to the"}, {"start": 1278.0, "text": "device from the core location"}, {"start": 1280.0, "text": "servers."}, {"start": 1281.0, "text": "Once this is done, while the"}, {"start": 1283.0, "text": "device Wi-Fi radio must be"}, {"start": 1284.0, "text": "active, it no longer needs a"}, {"start": 1286.0, "text": "network connection for"}, {"start": 1288.0, "text": "positioning to work."}, {"start": 1289.0, "text": "When an app calls location"}, {"start": 1291.0, "text": "accuracy best, the device"}, {"start": 1293.0, "text": "passively looks at the"}, {"start": 1294.0, "text": "fingerprint, does an on-device"}, {"start": 1296.0, "text": "pattern match, derives the"}, {"start": 1298.0, "text": "coordinates and plots the"}, {"start": 1299.0, "text": "location dots."}, {"start": 1301.0, "text": "Local sensors are then used to"}, {"start": 1302.0, "text": "keep the dot up to date until a"}, {"start": 1304.0, "text": "threshold at which point the"}, {"start": 1306.0, "text": "device looks at the fingerprint"}, {"start": 1307.0, "text": "again."}, {"start": 1308.0, "text": "Apple indoor positioning is"}, {"start": 1310.0, "text": "incredibly fast, low power and"}, {"start": 1312.0, "text": "private."}, {"start": 1313.0, "text": "In short, an indoor map plus"}, {"start": 1316.0, "text": "Wi-Fi gives you the blue dot."}, {"start": 1319.0, "text": "The specific steps to enable"}, {"start": 1321.0, "text": "indoor positioning are, with an"}, {"start": 1323.0, "text": "IMDF already loaded into your"}, {"start": 1325.0, "text": "account, collect the Wi-Fi using"}, {"start": 1327.0, "text": "the survey app, upload the"}, {"start": 1329.0, "text": "surveys back to the core"}, {"start": 1330.0, "text": "location servers for analysis"}, {"start": 1332.0, "text": "and activation, and then test"}, {"start": 1334.0, "text": "positioning in the survey app as"}, {"start": 1336.0, "text": "a reference for quality."}, {"start": 1337.0, "text": "Let's take a quick look at a"}, {"start": 1339.0, "text": "demonstration of surveying and"}, {"start": 1341.0, "text": "testing positioning."}, {"start": 1343.0, "text": "In the survey process, you drop"}, {"start": 1344.0, "text": "points on a screen as visual"}, {"start": 1346.0, "text": "markers of where you are"}, {"start": 1348.0, "text": "standing in the real world."}, {"start": 1349.0, "text": "This is how the positioning"}, {"start": 1350.0, "text": "algorithm is calibrated to your"}, {"start": 1352.0, "text": "location."}, {"start": 1354.0, "text": "Here, you can see the surveyor"}, {"start": 1355.0, "text": "has oriented himself in the room"}, {"start": 1358.0, "text": "and on the screen and then"}, {"start": 1359.0, "text": "presses record."}, {"start": 1361.0, "text": "The surveyor then moves the"}, {"start": 1362.0, "text": "crosshair to the next location"}, {"start": 1364.0, "text": "five to eight meters out to a"}, {"start": 1365.0, "text": "point he can verify."}, {"start": 1367.0, "text": "And when in that spot, taps on"}, {"start": 1368.0, "text": "the screen, registering the"}, {"start": 1370.0, "text": "point."}, {"start": 1371.0, "text": "Notice his feet crossed the grid"}, {"start": 1372.0, "text": "lines on the floor as he taps on"}, {"start": 1374.0, "text": "the screen and calibrates the"}, {"start": 1375.0, "text": "survey."}, {"start": 1377.0, "text": "At corners, the surveyor makes"}, {"start": 1379.0, "text": "right angle turns in place,"}, {"start": 1380.0, "text": "rotates the screen, taps and"}, {"start": 1382.0, "text": "walks."}, {"start": 1383.0, "text": "The area colored in represents"}, {"start": 1385.0, "text": "the Wi-Fi signal captured."}, {"start": 1387.0, "text": "When the floor is entirely"}, {"start": 1388.0, "text": "colored in, the area is"}, {"start": 1390.0, "text": "fingerprinted and the data is"}, {"start": 1391.0, "text": "ready for upload."}, {"start": 1393.0, "text": "Once the survey data has been"}, {"start": 1394.0, "text": "processed, you'll be notified"}, {"start": 1396.0, "text": "that the indoor positioning is"}, {"start": 1398.0, "text": "ready."}, {"start": 1399.0, "text": "Toggle privacy, location"}, {"start": 1401.0, "text": "services to flush the location"}, {"start": 1402.0, "text": "cache."}, {"start": 1404.0, "text": "And then you can begin testing"}, {"start": 1405.0, "text": "the accuracy of indoor"}, {"start": 1407.0, "text": "positioning."}, {"start": 1408.0, "text": "If positioning is working, the"}, {"start": 1410.0, "text": "map will display in test mode,"}, {"start": 1412.0, "text": "the green areas represent all"}, {"start": 1413.0, "text": "the surveys that were uploaded"}, {"start": 1415.0, "text": "and successfully processed."}, {"start": 1417.0, "text": "The blue dot is the center point"}, {"start": 1419.0, "text": "of the positioning estimate with"}, {"start": 1420.0, "text": "the light blue circle being the"}, {"start": 1422.0, "text": "range of confidence in accuracy."}, {"start": 1424.0, "text": "Here, you can see the confidence"}, {"start": 1427.0, "text": "circle is well within the three"}, {"start": 1428.0, "text": "to five meter expectation of"}, {"start": 1430.0, "text": "Apple indoor positioning and is"}, {"start": 1432.0, "text": "following the tester quite well"}, {"start": 1434.0, "text": "in the smaller environment."}, {"start": 1435.0, "text": "Including fixtures such as the"}, {"start": 1437.0, "text": "tables in your IMDF will add to"}, {"start": 1439.0, "text": "the constraints placed on the"}, {"start": 1440.0, "text": "positioning service and enhance"}, {"start": 1442.0, "text": "accuracy."}, {"start": 1444.0, "text": "Let's recap how indoor"}, {"start": 1445.0, "text": "positioning works and how we"}, {"start": 1447.0, "text": "enable it."}, {"start": 1448.0, "text": "Apple indoor positioning uses"}, {"start": 1450.0, "text": "Wi-Fi fingerprinting."}, {"start": 1452.0, "text": "It uses any Wi-Fi signal in the"}, {"start": 1454.0, "text": "building passively and does not"}, {"start": 1456.0, "text": "make any impact on the network."}, {"start": 1458.0, "text": "Indoor positioning is enabled"}, {"start": 1460.0, "text": "using the indoor survey app and"}, {"start": 1462.0, "text": "the IMDF made available through"}, {"start": 1464.0, "text": "the Indoor Maps Program."}, {"start": 1466.0, "text": "Surveying isn't difficult but"}, {"start": 1468.0, "text": "the steps have to be followed if"}, {"start": 1469.0, "text": "you are to succeed."}, {"start": 1471.0, "text": "Everyone surveying a location"}, {"start": 1473.0, "text": "should have the same model of"}, {"start": 1475.0, "text": "iPhone and same version of iOS."}, {"start": 1477.0, "text": "Drop pins every five to eight"}, {"start": 1479.0, "text": "meters as you walk and continue"}, {"start": 1481.0, "text": "in smooth motion."}, {"start": 1483.0, "text": "Keep in the center of walkways"}, {"start": 1484.0, "text": "to ensure the walls are factored"}, {"start": 1486.0, "text": "in to your positioning"}, {"start": 1487.0, "text": "constraints."}, {"start": 1488.0, "text": "Do not use any sort of case on"}, {"start": 1490.0, "text": "your iPhone while surveying."}, {"start": 1492.0, "text": "And read the help documentation"}, {"start": 1494.0, "text": "for tips on patterns to walk for"}, {"start": 1497.0, "text": "enabling specific types of"}, {"start": 1498.0, "text": "buildings and positioning use"}, {"start": 1500.0, "text": "cases."}, {"start": 1501.0, "text": "Finally, now that we have an"}, {"start": 1503.0, "text": "IMDF and indoor positioning, how"}, {"start": 1506.0, "text": "do we put this in our apps and"}, {"start": 1507.0, "text": "websites?"}, {"start": 1509.0, "text": "MapKit and MapKit JS support"}, {"start": 1511.0, "text": "decoding and rendering of"}, {"start": 1513.0, "text": "GeoJSON files."}, {"start": 1514.0, "text": "You can use these frameworks to"}, {"start": 1516.0, "text": "display IMDF data as overlays"}, {"start": 1518.0, "text": "and annotations on a map."}, {"start": 1521.0, "text": "Styling your indoor map elements"}, {"start": 1523.0, "text": "is critical to how the map is"}, {"start": 1524.0, "text": "perceived and used."}, {"start": 1526.0, "text": "Apply styles that match your"}, {"start": 1528.0, "text": "app's theme or your company's"}, {"start": 1529.0, "text": "brand."}, {"start": 1530.0, "text": "For a rich indoor experience,"}, {"start": 1533.0, "text": "you can take advantage of indoor"}, {"start": 1535.0, "text": "location by enabling Apple"}, {"start": 1537.0, "text": "indoor positioning within your"}, {"start": 1538.0, "text": "building and then using APIs"}, {"start": 1541.0, "text": "from the core location framework"}, {"start": 1543.0, "text": "to display the user location"}, {"start": 1544.0, "text": "indoors."}, {"start": 1545.0, "text": "To learn more, check out the"}, {"start": 1547.0, "text": "video and sample code for our"}, {"start": 1549.0, "text": "WWDC Session Adding Indoor Maps"}, {"start": 1552.0, "text": "to your App and Website."}, {"start": 1555.0, "text": "And that's the Indoor Maps"}, {"start": 1556.0, "text": "Program."}, {"start": 1557.0, "text": "We look forward to seeing all"}, {"start": 1558.0, "text": "the wonderful apps you will"}, {"start": 1559.0, "text": "build."}, {"start": 1560.0, "text": "Thank you so much for your time"}, {"start": 1562.0, "text": "today. For more information, visit our"}, {"start": 1564.0, "text": "website at"}]}
